<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Only pages a signed-out visitor can actually read belong here. Everything
  behind authentication redirects to the login page, so listing it would offer
  a crawler nothing but a redirect, and the transactional pages (password
  reset, email confirmation) are single-use links rather than content.

  Shared lists are public but user-owned and private by default, so they are
  deliberately left out of the site's own sitemap.

  The pages for films and series are not listed here. The backend serves the
  sitemap index at /sitemap.xml, which names this file and the title sitemaps
  it builds from the catalogue.

  No lastmod: a hand-maintained date that drifts is worse than none, because a
  crawler that learns the dates are wrong stops trusting them.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
